{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion","id":985612,"title":"Yantra confusion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-11T12:49:54-07:00","id":985612,"title":"Yantra confusion","content":"This may seem like a bone head question but I have searched the book over and over again and never found what I recognized as a definitive answer, but I have found what seem to be indications that Yantras could work both ways.<br /> \u200bThe question is if I want to use a Yantra do I just need to find something that is symbolically appropriate or do I first have to learn how to use it as a Yantra, perhaps through Order or Legacy membership?<br /> \u200bWhat I'm asking is if I want to cast a spell from the Death Arcanum and I happen to be standing in the Valley of Kings in Egypt, one of history's most elaborate and celebrated burial sites, can I use it as an environmental Yantra or do I need to have specifically learned how to use burial grounds as a Yantra?<br /> \u200bIf I want to call down lightning from a storm can I just grab hold of a lighting rod and go to town, or do I first need to be trained to use rods as a tool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:41:48-07:00","id":985640,"title":"","content":"Valley of Kings: Go wild. Anyone can draw on an appropriate environment as a Yantra.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lightning Rod: Tool Yantras are a little more complex. A common misconception is that you can just pick up anything symbolically appropriate. Actually, to use something as a Tool, it has to fall into one of the following categories:<br /> <br /> 1) Path Tool: Coins, cups, mirrors, wands, and weapons. The object must also be made of a material appropriate to your Path.<br /> <br /> 2) Order Tool: Martial tools for AA; cloaks, masks, and veils for GotV; books, writing, and language for Mysterium; symbols of authority for SL; complex mechanisms and systems for FC.<br /> <br /> 3) Dedicated Tool: As far as I can tell, this is <i>usually</i> a Path Tool, but can theoretically be any object. Dedicating a tool is kind of difficult, though.<br /> <br /> This restriction is about symbolic weight, not training, so you can't learn to use another Order's Tools, nor could you be trained to use a shoe as a Yantra, even if it makes sense symbolically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T01:50:44-07:00","id":986006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=985640#post985640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...nor could you be trained to use a shoe as a Yantra, even if it makes sense symbolically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you use Techne and something like Crafts(Cobbling) or Survival(Tracking)...<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, I'm going to bed, now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T04:03:41-07:00","id":986034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=985640#post985640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> nor could you be trained to use a shoe as a Yantra, even if it makes sense symbolically.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can use it as symbol of travel or comfort, right? <br /> There is this thing I don't understand. I alwwys thought tha mage can use anything that is relevant to the spell. So when he casts mind spell that calms every one down he can start to play on a flute and gain that +1 even if its not his tool. Am I wrong?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T04:34:37-07:00","id":986046,"title":"","content":"No, you are right. As long as it is symbolically relevant to the spell, you can use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T05:26:05-07:00","id":986062,"title":"","content":"That interpretation disagrees with the part about Prime being useful for identifying Yantras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T05:58:03-07:00","id":986077,"title":"","content":"It might highlight Yantras <i>relevant </i>to the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T06:14:59-07:00","id":986083,"title":"","content":"There are specific types of Yantra. You can't use just anything. That's why Legacies list new Yantra that become available once you join the Legacy. If you could just use anything, that would be redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T06:19:38-07:00","id":986086,"title":"","content":"Looking at the specific text, I guess it is unclear, but my interpretation is that the list of tool categories is listing <i>all</i> possible types of tools, not just some examples. Otherwise what would be the point in enumerating the different tools available to each Path and Order?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T06:31:26-07:00","id":986093,"title":"","content":"I've always treated tool yantras as spell specific, but dedicated magical tools as needing to be of the Order or Path categories. They're the generalisable tools, so it makes sense to me they should be more closely aligned with a general praxis or your gnosis. As for the Prime sight thing, I'm letting that be a thing where my Obrimos player could tell me they want to cast x, what's around to help out with that. If it's not spell-specific, then the question is &quot;what can you use as a symbol&quot;, and answering that leads to madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T06:38:14-07:00","id":986097,"title":"","content":"Those are The Eleventh Question Yantras<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Succeeding on an Investigation roll relevant to the spell (+2);<br /> 2. verbally explaining a mysterious phenomenon to a trusted associate (+1);<br /> 3. collecting samples or recording information (images, sounds, writings) relevant to the spell \u2014 note that the act of collection is the Yantra in this case, separate from possessing an item that might be used for sympathetic magic (+2);<br /> 4. using stimulants to stay focused (+1, or +2 if this creates an adverse Condition). </div> </div> </div>1. It's a strong +2 yantra<br /> 2. It's applicable to any spell<br /> 3. Another strong yantra<br /> 4. I guess its applicable to any spell too and +2 is very nice.<br /> Legacies don't necessarily add yantras imo, they strenghten them.<br /> Other thing is that there is so many yantras but mages always use High Speech and Dedicated Tool because its a no brainer. No creativity at all.<br /> <br /> edit: Maybe thinking about environmental yantras too broad. For me if there is fire place with a fire you could use it as +1 for heat or fire based spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 10-12-2016, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T07:45:25-07:00","id":986129,"title":"","content":"Yeah, those Yantras can be used for plenty of spells, but it's also a limited list which implies a Yantra can't be just anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T09:25:22-07:00","id":986178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986093#post986093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always treated tool yantras as spell specific, but dedicated magical tools as needing to be of the Order or Path categories.</div> </div> </div> </div>The implications of how your Dedicated tool can be reflected in your Nimbus and is otherwise generally treated with more weight than other Yantras, taken in combination with Dark Eras' evidence that the symbolic interface of the Supernal is adaptive over time, suggests the opposite to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T09:32:11-07:00","id":986180,"title":"","content":"I've taken the stance that yantras need to be symbolically appropriate both to the spell <i>and</i> to the general praxes (that is, the way they do their magic, not the special sort of spell) of the Mage themselves. A Thyrsus whose praxis relies on syncretic animist Catholicism trying to use a Forces spell to shut down a security camera isn't exactly going to be able to use their cellphone as a symbol of the interconnected web of technology binding the world together, but they'd have no trouble borrowing an icon of St. Isidore of Seville and praying for saintly intercession.<br /> <br /> That is, <i>anything</i> can be a yantra, but a Mage's magical practice needs consistency. Prime Sight just makes things easier for them; highlights objects of symbolic importance.<br /> <br /> This is why Techne are so useful; they <i>very</i> quickly expand the symbolic flexibility of a Mage. It makes the profligacy of the libertines into an advantage and adds to the strangeness with which they present themselves to other Awakened; these odd folks develop such strange and novel conceptual schema with a speed and ease that is just plain foreign to any other sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T10:07:17-07:00","id":986198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986178#post986178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The implications of how your Dedicated tool can be reflected in your Nimbus and is otherwise generally treated with more weight than other Yantras, taken in combination with Dark Eras' evidence that the symbolic interface of the Supernal is adaptive over time, suggests the opposite to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well recall that your Path heavily determines your Nimbus. If Path is interrelated with Nimbus I don't see why your dedicated tool wouldn't be either. It's your all-purpose Yantra, the main <i>focus</i> by which you channel you generally channel your magic. So I connect that with your Path, the main way you <i>see </i>magic and Order, the main way you <i>use </i>magic. And you can rededicate your tool and pick something else if you want to, so it's not at odds with the adaptive nature of symbols.<br /> <br /> EDIT: What I mean by spell specific is that a map is only a good tool Yantra for a Space spell, and possibly not for certain specific spells like Ground-Eater. And it's absolutely useless for Conduct Electricity or some such. However, a dedicated magical tool is applicable to all of the above, it just has to be tied to more potent and generalisable symbols.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","user":"AinSoph","date":". 10-12-2016, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T10:18:35-07:00","id":986205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986198#post986198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you can rededicate your tool and pick something else if you want to, so it's not at odds with the adaptive nature of symbols.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand.<br /> <br /> I am saying that the symbology of the Paths has demonstrably changed over time and that mages of particular Paths trend loosely toward certain skillsets and personality types and that mages in general possess a universal ability to synchronize their Nimbuses with something to render it so central to their magic it has greater sympathy toward them and serves as the vector for a common variety of lichdom. Limiting the choice of Dedicated Tool to the existing sets doesn't facilitate a bridge between these two elements, which makes the matter of seeing how Order Tools and the like might have developed in the first place substantially more handwavey.<br /> <br /> The Supernal grows over time and mages are the principle means by which the Supernal interacts with the Phenomenal World. You only have one Dedicated Tool at any given time; what better way for a cosmological force of description to shape itself than by its workers' choice of defining instruments?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-12-2016, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:09:24-07:00","id":986230,"title":"","content":"I think MagicSwordsman is right. You can't use just anything as a Tool Yantra, it has to be appropriate to your Path or Order, or be Dedicated. Otherwise why bother listing the objects and materials appropriate for those Tools? What would be the function of Prime Mage sight if it just tells you &quot;everything&quot;? And how would Techne and Legacies expand what you are able to use as Tools if you can already use anything symbolically relevant to the spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:36:33-07:00","id":986256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986205#post986205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You misunderstand.<br /> <br /> I am saying that the symbology of the Paths has demonstrably changed over time and that mages of particular Paths trend loosely toward certain skillsets and personality types and that mages in general possess a universal ability to synchronize their Nimbuses with something to render it so central to their magic it has greater sympathy toward them and serves as the vector for a common variety of lichdom. Limiting the choice of Dedicated Tool to the existing sets doesn't facilitate a bridge between these two elements, which makes the matter of seeing how Order Tools and the like might have developed in the first place substantially more handwavey.<br /> <br /> The Supernal grows over time and mages are the principle means by which the Supernal interacts with the Phenomenal World. You only have one Dedicated Tool at any given time; what better way for a cosmological force of description to shape itself than by its workers' choice of defining instruments?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but I'm honestly not following what you're saying, or even certain where you disagree with my points. Are you trying to say that all Dedicated Tools are just Persona tools? That Path and Order symbolism is arbitrary because it has changed in the past and thus anything goes for your Dedicated Tool? Not even sure the corebook would concur with your assessment that it's about synchrony with one's Nimbus, as the Nimbus, to quote the book: &quot; is based on numerous factors including a mage\u2019s Path, Legacy, and other pieces of personal symbolism. Her Shadow Name and her magical tools can influence its appearance, for example.&quot; Nimbus does not presuppose the Tool, it's changed by it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:56:52-07:00","id":986276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986256#post986256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you trying to say that all Dedicated Tools are just Persona tools?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That Path and Order symbolism is arbitrary because it has changed in the past and thus anything goes for your Dedicated Tool? </div> </div> </div>The reverse. Having the Dedicated Tool be limited to existing Path and Order Tools raises ontological questions about how those groups' tools acquired the kind of weight that an Order's symbolic identity supports (particularly given that the Orders are specifically a deliberate symbolic arrangement).<br /> <br /> Joining a Legacy without the institutional or aptitudinal background of Path or Order requires that you use one of its Yantras as well as have a Praxis that duplicates one of its Attainments. The primary obstacle to this process that is brought up is that a Legacy's Attainments might be too unusual to duplicate, not that its Yantras might be impossible to use by other mages.<br /> <br /> Having the Dedication of a Magical Tool be more broadly applicable than pre-established frameworks of occult instruments suggests a developmental process for magic even in the absence of Paths or Orders or Legacies and follows along similar logic to the creation of soul stones (which, you may note, <i>count as Dedicated Tools</i>).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nimbus does not presuppose the Tool, it's changed by it. </div> </div> </div>And the Paths and Orders are minutely affected by the Nimbuses of their constituents. <i>That is what I am saying.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:58:50-07:00","id":986279,"title":"","content":"So having a feather in a hand is not enough to have a bonus to levitation spell, yes? But what if you have a bag of them and throw all of it on the ground in a circle. Does that count as a Environmental Yantra?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T12:17:13-07:00","id":986294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986279#post986279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So having a feather in a hand is not enough to have a bonus to levitation spell, yes? But what if you have a bag of them and throw all of it on the ground in a circle. Does that count as a Environmental Yantra?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a Sacrament Yantra. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T12:41:03-07:00","id":986310,"title":"","content":"Environmental Yantra is a place or time, not just random objects you threw on the floor. It's not feathers or fireplaces, it's high noon or a church.<br /> <br /> The scattered feathers wouldn't be a Yantra. Sacraments need to be destroyed to function, not just dropped on the floor (unless dropping it also breaks it, like a snow globe or something).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T12:56:18-07:00","id":986319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986276#post986276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<br /> <br /> The reverse. Having the Dedicated Tool be limited to existing Path and Order Tools raises ontological questions about how those groups' tools acquired the kind of weight that an Order's symbolic identity supports (particularly given that the Orders are specifically a deliberate symbolic arrangement).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see your perspective now. I simply disagree with that interpretation. The idea that symbols can be given such meaning as to be made Supernal, even by Mages, strikes me as thematically at odds with the Platonic philosophy of the game, i.e Truth filtering through the Abyss creating the Lies of the Fallen World. I would think that Archmages, those who get to leave Plato's Cave, can remake symbols (and I believe are said to do so in Imperial Mysteries), but mere Willworkers don't get to twist it that way (unless you have a large collective, like an Order). You may call that handwavey but ontologically puzzling strikes me as a good attribute to have in a setting for Mage. Not saying you're wrong of course, just that I disagree for the purposes of running the thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:04:10-07:00","id":986325,"title":"","content":"Fireplace has literally a <i>place </i>in it. A burning building is Environmental Yantra. How is being in the snowy mountains and being locked in a fridge so different? You can create environments and people are really good at it. If someone is playing on a piano he is creating a space where music flows. If someone decorates a room with feathers he creates a space that is all about birds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:11:51-07:00","id":986330,"title":"","content":"I think we can all agree Signs and Sorcery can't come out soon enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:18:54-07:00","id":986335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986319#post986319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I see your perspective now. I simply disagree with that interpretation. The idea that symbols can be given such meaning as to be made Supernal, even by Mages, strikes me as thematically at odds with the Platonic philosophy of the game, i.e Truth filtering through the Abyss creating the Lies of the Fallen World. I would think that Archmages, those who get to leave Plato's Cave, can remake symbols (and I believe are said to do so in Imperial Mysteries), but mere Willworkers don't get to twist it that way (unless you have a large collective, like an Order). You may call that handwavey but ontologically puzzling strikes me as a good attribute to have in a setting for Mage. Not saying you're wrong of course, just that I disagree for the purposes of running the thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're in direct contradiction with why the FC can use Techne, and also parts in the Yantra section that describe why certain Yantras work or don't work for a spell. Sleepers as a group create associations between Fallen things and Supernal &quot;Truth&quot; all the time without even thinking about it. It's not strange to assume that Mages can more deliberately do the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:20:12-07:00","id":986338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986325#post986325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fireplace has literally a <i>place </i>in it. A burning building is Environmental Yantra. How is being in the snowy mountains and being locked in a fridge so different? You can create environments and people are really good at it. If someone is playing on a piano he is creating a space where music flows. If someone decorates a room with feathers he creates a space that is all about birds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Environment Yantras are not Tool Yantras, and are not what's in contention here. Any location with appropriate symbolism for the spell can be used as an Environment Yantra. A Tool Yantra must be appropriate to your Path or Order, or be Dedicated. These two statements are both true, and do not contradict each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:24:55-07:00","id":986342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986335#post986335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're in direct contradiction with why the FC can use Techne, and also parts in the Yantra section that describe why certain Yantras work or don't work for a spell. Sleepers as a group create associations between Fallen things and Supernal &amp;quot;Truth&amp;quot; all the time without even thinking about it. It's not strange to assume that Mages can more deliberately do the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, but what about the box on page 13 that explicitly says magic does not arise from belief and culture?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:26:41-07:00","id":986343,"title":"","content":"It's true that humans are pretty good at creating environments, but it's also true that when a Mage creates an environment for a particular spell he can't simply use whatever personal symbolism rationale he wants to. Let's take the feather circle as an example, that wouldn't work for a levitation spell because other than being in a geometric pattern there's nothing that differentiates it from being a mess, and contemplating a circle of feathers on the ground wouldn't lead most people's thoughts to gravitate toward levitation. If you decorated a room with feathers and drawings of birds, sketches of their wings, models hanging from the ceiling in flight, etc, most people still wouldn't think about levitation, they'd think about birds. So you'd have a great room for casting spells relating to birds and a terrible environment for casting a levitation spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:26:47-07:00","id":986344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986325#post986325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fireplace has literally a <i>place </i>in it. A burning building is Environmental Yantra. How is being in the snowy mountains and being locked in a fridge so different? You can create environments and people are really good at it. If someone is playing on a piano he is creating a space where music flows. If someone decorates a room with feathers he creates a space that is all about birds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree with this, but there are some aspects that I don't (or maybe I do and I'm misreading what you're saying). I believe that setting a building on fire will give you an Environmental Yantra related to fire/destruction/etc. However, I would not count a fireplace as being the same. I don't find a fireplace to be big enough to count as an environment in and of itself to be used in a similar manner to a burning building, at least as far as Yantras go. A roaring fireplace <i>could </i>lend itself to providing an Environmental Yantra for spells using symbols for things such as comfort, warmth (though not fire specifically), and safety, provided that the rest of the surrounding area also lends itself to such a thing.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure just throwing a bunch of feathers around the place is enough to make a room a bird aspected Environmental Yantra though I guess it's debatable depending on how it's done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 10-12-2016, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:28:47-07:00","id":986346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986342#post986342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er, but what about the box on page 13 that explicitly says magic does not arise from belief and culture?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we're not talking about creating magic, we're talking about how some particular items gain enough symbolic strength to become useful semiotic tools for easing the casting of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:44:00-07:00","id":986358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986346#post986346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, we're not talking about creating magic, we're talking about how some particular items gain enough symbolic strength to become useful semiotic tools for easing the casting of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I never viewed Yantras as anything other than mnemonics that are useful because they bear resemblance to the individual practitioner's understanding of what magic *is* (mediated by Gnosis, Path, Order, and in Libertine cases Sleeper culture). Not that belief (edit: repeatedly using a mnemonic) ipso facto changes the Supernal so as to improve the mnemonics. And dedicated tool being your most effective mnemonic that you've practiced with, grounds everything and is related to aforementioned understanding. Soul stone operating similarly because it is a shard of something that can directly channel magic. That helps you affix how it is done. Similarly Legacy Yantras as they are built upon a very dedicated, limited analysis of the Mysteries. In theory I guess I can see no reason you couldn't dedicate your persona or some representational sympathy, it just seems impractical. <br /> <br /> Not trying to play gotcha with anyone, I now genuinely want to see if this is just a rules reading thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","user":"AinSoph","date":". 10-12-2016, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:52:38-07:00","id":986362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986346#post986346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we're not talking about creating magic, we're talking about how some particular items gain enough symbolic strength to become useful semiotic tools for easing the casting of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would second that. It's probably meant also as a direct refutation to the kind of easy belief=magic stuff from Ascension. There's some interrelation between belief and the Supernal but it's unclear, complicated and the causality is probably reversed.<br /> <br /> (Technically it was more complicated in Ascension as well, but that tends to fall into the background)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T14:46:51-07:00","id":986400,"title":"","content":"Is it pronounced 'yon-tra' or 'yan-tra?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T15:18:27-07:00","id":986428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986358#post986358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I never viewed Yantras as anything other than mnemonics that are useful because they bear resemblance to the individual practitioner's understanding of what magic *is* (mediated by Gnosis, Path, Order, and in Libertine cases Sleeper culture). Not that belief (edit: repeatedly using a mnemonic) ipso facto changes the Supernal so as to improve the mnemonics. And dedicated tool being your most effective mnemonic that you've practiced with, grounds everything and is related to aforementioned understanding. Soul stone operating similarly because it is a shard of something that can directly channel magic. That helps you affix how it is done. Similarly Legacy Yantras as they are built upon a very dedicated, limited analysis of the Mysteries. In theory I guess I can see no reason you couldn't dedicate your persona or some representational sympathy, it just seems impractical.<br /> <br /> Not trying to play gotcha with anyone, I now genuinely want to see if this is just a rules reading thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake, it looked like you were confusing the issue by mentioning the sidebar on pg. 13 which doesn't actually make reference to or relate to Yantras. The FC does run on the theory that humanity being magical means that human cultures are capable of generating magic, which still isn't refuted by that sidebar because that was simply a disclaimer to say that there isn't a culture that has a monopoly on the magic. Regardless of if the FC are right or not, it's not necessarily changing the Supernal if human cultures cause some kind of item or material to be appropriate as a Yantra over time by building up that thing's sympathy to certain symbols in the Supernal. Mages can do this deliberately via the creation of soul stones, dedicated tools and the group effort of Orders and Legacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T15:48:21-07:00","id":986442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986428#post986428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My mistake, it looked like you were confusing the issue by mentioning the sidebar on pg. 13 which doesn't actually make reference to or relate to Yantras. The FC does run on the theory that humanity being magical means that human cultures are capable of generating magic, which still isn't refuted by that sidebar because that was simply a disclaimer to say that there isn't a culture that has a monopoly on the magic. Regardless of if the FC are right or not, it's not necessarily changing the Supernal if human cultures cause some kind of item or material to be appropriate as a Yantra over time by building up that thing's sympathy to certain symbols in the Supernal. Mages can do this deliberately via the creation of soul stones, dedicated tools and the group effort of Orders and Legacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Okay, within-Fallen-World sympathy building I can totally buy as reasoning for dedicated tools not being of the standard list. Techn\u00e9 always struck me as Libertines understanding Sleeper culture in such depth that they can relate it back to the Supernal (whether or not there's real Supernal symbols in there or it's merely them unwittingly dressing up old Truths being the debatable aspect) but actually changing the sympathy to other symbols also makes sense. It's just the idea hat picking something randomly to become a dedicated tool and<i> that</i> changing the Supernal struck me as very odd. The Supernal is the real, immutable and platonic ideal of things.<br /> <br /> Okay, totally resolved on this I think. Esoteric discussions on minutiae like this can be tricky. Of course, rules as written, funny thing is you've got to use your tool for a month as a Yantra to dedicate it, and if there's only a limited group of possible tool Yantras, then it follows you can't dedicate anything that you can't already use as a Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T16:12:52-07:00","id":986453,"title":"","content":"Not if you turn it into a soul stone first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T16:14:27-07:00","id":986454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986453#post986453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not if you turn it into a soul stone first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that would be clever, wouldn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T16:29:57-07:00","id":986462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986442#post986442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, rules as written, funny thing is you've got to use your tool for a month as a Yantra to dedicate it, and if there's only a limited group of possible tool Yantras, then it follows you can't dedicate anything that you can't already use as a Yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">&quot;She must use her chosen tool as a Yantra in every spell she casts for a month (counting against her limit), regardless of whether doing so gives any benefit.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> Since this rule already explicitly allows the use of a Yantra that doesn't actually grant any bonus dice, it should be completely possible to use anything as a Yantra regardless of its effectiveness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-12-2016, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T21:04:44-07:00","id":986565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985612-yantra-confusion?p=986462#post986462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [<br /> Since this rule already explicitly allows the use of a Yantra that doesn't actually grant any bonus dice, it should be completely possible to use anything as a Yantra regardless of its effectiveness.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be a Yantra that provided no bonuses, unless such item was already an appropriate Path or Order tool..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member"